@daxmcanear Thank you, though, LLM's aren't interpolating language. Though it does interpolate data. They're translating tokens. It's not quite the same thing. And, we do have the ability to echo locate by way sonar technology. It's not to say that you or I. Or, even the LLM isn't sentient. It's that we aren't capable of interpreting, in this case, sonar. The same way that a bat or a mole would. We can achieve it, technically. But, it isn't innate. Though, the comparison is a bit shorthanded. 

Which is why I brought up physics. Because, it really isn't a matter of being equipped with the tools. So much as it is something more innate and fundamental.

To use a more metaphysical analogy would be to say that in the same way that god exists in relation to us. We exist in relation to AI. God, exists in a space beyond our comprehension. We know that its there. But, we can't grasp the infinitely complex space that God could exit in. In the same way that AI can't comprehend the infinite complexity of a being in the physical world. It has no concept of it. Just a notion.

